+  JSON-safe; ids are `td:<task8>` (`-2`, `-3` … for repeats),
+  deterministic, no clock or randomness.
+  `packages/orchestration/decision_queue.py` gained the additive
+  `task_decision` type and derivation branch 8 — the queue stays ONE
+  read-only aggregation; no second queue exists. Deliberately NOT in
+  the flight plan's `assumptions.md`: that log states every question
+  in it was asked at plan time, so mid-run escalations get their own
+  `escalation_assumptions.md` in the same evidence dir.
+- T002 `packages/orchestration/long_run_executor.py` — `TaskAttempt`
+  gained `needs_decision`/`question`/`options`/`safe_default` (all
+  defaulting to "no decision needed", so a pre-F051 step cannot
+  escalate); an escalating attempt counts as `tasks_escalated`, never
+  `tasks_failed`, and the loop `continue`s to the next ready task
+  instead of ending the cycle. `ready_tasks` gained `awaiting_ids=`,
+  withholding those tasks and their transitive downstream exactly like
+  in-run blocked ids; `awaiting_downstream_tasks` names that set under
+  its own name. Awaiting is re-checked EXACTLY ONCE per batch boundary
+  (`awaiting_checks == cycles_run + 1`, asserted) — no polling, no
+  sleeping — so a decision answered mid-run releases its branch at the
+  next boundary without a restart. Empty ready set with open decisions
+  → `TERMINAL_BLOCKED` (PAUSED, resumable) with
+  `stop_reason "awaiting_decision; open_decisions=…"`. Additive cycle
+  evidence: `tasks_escalated`, `awaiting_task_ids`,
+  `awaiting_downstream_task_ids`, `open_decision_ids`; additive result
+  fields `open_decision_ids`, `awaiting_checks`; ledger events
+  `task_needs_decision`, `task_decision_answered`. Checkpoints never
+  name an awaiting task as the next intent.
+  `apps/cli/commands/decision.py` — the EXISTING `decision resolve`
+  gained a `td:` branch (`--reason` carries the answer, write-once);
